// Fixture: op_statement_parens_basic
// Rule under test: GDDL Spec v4 §6.3 -- explicit parentheses are available for grouping
// whenever a particular grouping is wanted, on top of the base strict left-to-right
// evaluation rule. SIBLING-BUG FIXTURE: the evaluator rewrite that fixed the left-to-
// right precedence bug specifically added real paren-grouping via recursion -- that is
// new code with zero prior coverage in this corpus. This fixture is the basic sanity
// check that parenthesized grouping parses and evaluates correctly at all.
//
// Note: for THIS particular arrangement, the parenthesized grouping happens to produce
// the same result strict left-to-right would already give without any parens (grouping
// the leftmost operator pair first is what left-to-right does by default anyway). That
// means this fixture alone cannot prove parens are doing anything beyond what left-to-
// right already does -- it only proves the paren-recursion code path executes and
// evaluates correctly. The fixture that actually proves grouping changes the outcome is
// op_statement_parens_override_left_to_right.gddl, which deliberately groups a NON-
// adjacent-by-default pair of operations to force a different result.

define Creature
	hitpoints_maximum = f32

Creature Base
	hitpoints_maximum = 100

Creature Derived = Base
	hitpoints_maximum = (20 + hitpoints_maximum) * 0.5

// Expected (prediction, pending golden output from Compiler Core reference run):
//   Derived.hitpoints_maximum == 60.0
//   ( (20 + 100) * 0.5 = 120 * 0.5 = 60.0 )
